lines=['# Evidence and operating limits','',f'The current reference corpus has {profile["corpus_papers"]} usable historical English theoretical-physics papers. Only the {profile["discovery_papers"]} discovery papers supply reference distributions and rule-development evidence; {profile["heldout_papers"]} remain held out.','', '## What was actually examined','', '- Initial sample:15 discovery papers,60 formula-centered windows,360 labels;59 main-body windows and1 appendix window. This evidence produced the frozen first skill.','- Additional sample:12 different discovery papers,60 windows,360 labels, category/year-band stratification with five role-preferred targets per paper.26 targets contain a display and34 are prose-only. The selected section labels are13 introduction,9 discussion/conclusion,38 technical body. Local neighboring paragraphs may overlap.','- Combined inventory:27 papers,120 windows,720 labels. This is an inventory total, not a pooled prevalence denominator. The added sample deliberately broadens paragraph functions.','', 'All six features were assigned by host agents who read the supplied source contexts. Exact quotations, version identity, line ranges and frozen contexts are machine-validated; quotations/full source stay in the local project cache. These are not human gold labels. The sample is not evidence that a strategy improves reading.','', '| Feature | Additional-window labels | Applicable yes/no papers |','|---|---|---:|']
